gh ground"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.6,"stats":{"hp":5500,"atk":200,"def":200,"res":10,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":5}},"eggcradler_fowlbeast":{"slug":"eggcradler_fowlbeast","name":"Eggcradler Fowlbeast","icon":"/enemies-icons/Eggcradler Fowlbeast.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Ranged","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Fowlbeasts indigenous to Kjerag, clutching their eggs tightly with powerful claws. The eggs never drop or break. Rhine Lab bionics researchers are studying them in the hope of developing a new type of stabilizer.","abilities":["Loses egg after being shifted, gaining Movement Speed and becoming unblockable"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.7,"stats":{"hp":7500,"atk":300,"def":150,"res":15,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":3.5}},"fluffy_snowball":{"slug":"fluffy_snowball","name":"Fluffy Snowball","icon":"/enemies-icons/Fluffy Snowball.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Creatures indigenous to Kjerag, popular amongst tourists for their soft, fluffy fur and friendly nature. Some claim that their fur was once the main clothing material for the people of Kjerag, but there is no evidence to verify this claim.","abilities":["Absorbs passing Snowchildren to increase its weight, HP, ATK, DEF, and RES","Returns to initial form on colliding with high ground"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.8,"stats":{"hp":5500,"atk":200,"def":200,"res":10,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":5}},"snowcap":{"slug":"snowcap","name":"Snowcap","icon":"/enemies-icons/Snowcap.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Ranged","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Large, umbrella-shaped mushrooms. They accumulate nutrients from spring through autumn, then grow rapidly in winter, reaching nearly a meter tall in two weeks. A favorite ingredient in Kjerag cheese fondue.","abilities":["Cannot be shifted","[Takes Root] at specific locations, causing its tile to become undeployable","[Takes Root] Reduces damage taken and protects all units behind it from avalanches"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":1,"stats":{"hp":12000,"atk":500,"def":600,"res":0,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":3.5}},"frostdillo":{"slug":"frostdillo","name":"Frostdillo","icon":"/enemies-icons/Frostdillo.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Creatures with heavy shells on their backs. Despite their intimidating appearance, they are actually docile and friendly and can be trained to serve as burdenbeasts. They can get back on their feet even when flipped on their backs.","abilities":["Loses all DEF and RES and becomes unable to move for some time on colliding with high ground"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.5,"stats":{"hp":8000,"atk":500,"def":3200,"res":80,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":3}},"greathorn_rhuul":{"slug":"greathorn_rhuul","name":"Greathorn Rhuul","icon":"/enemies-icons/Greathorn Rhuul.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Burdenbeasts with massive horns on their heads. Their unique name comes from Kjeragandr's blessing. It is said that someone once witnessed Her mumbling to this creature: 'Rhuul, rhuul...' Since then, 'Rhuul' has become its new name.","abilities":["[Clash of Brawn] Performs Charged Attacks and tries to push units that block it","After charging, deals damage to the target and pushes it back one tile; if unable to push, deals more damage and stuns the target for several seconds","Charge can be interrupted by negative statuses like Stun and Shift"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.7,"stats":{"hp":15000,"atk":800,"def":500,"res":20,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":5}},"isbit":{"slug":"isbit","name":"Isbit","icon":"/enemies-icons/Isbit.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Icy rock giants with a mind of their own. The name 'Isbit' means 'ice cube' in Kjeragi. Kjeragi legends say that frozen rocks turn into giants to throw intruders off the side of Mount Karlan. The tale has proven effective at dissuading children from climbing Karlan on their own.","abilities":["Attacks deal splash damage","Loses HP proportional to distance moved when shifted"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.3,"stats":{"hp":20000,"atk":1500,"def":2500,"res":80,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":7}}},"dropIcons":{"4002":"/item-icons/originite_prime.png","31053":"/item-icons/compound_cutting_fluid.png","act46side_token_detector":"/item-icons/multi_functional_snow_detector.png"},"previewFile":"os-9.webp","emergency":null,"devices":[{"col":4,"description":"Enemies increase the Avalanche Warning Index when entering the Avalanche Area Deploying Operators within the area will also increase the Index's value","hidden":false,"key":"trap_265_xdice1","kind":"device","name":"Saintess Statue","row":4},{"col":7,"description":"Enemies increase the Avalanche Warning Index when entering the Avalanche Area Deploying Operators within the area will also increase the Index's value","hidden":false,"key":"trap_265_xdice1","kind":"device","name":"Saintess Statue","row":4},{"col":8,"description":null,"hidden":false,"key":"trap_264_xdplat","kind":"device","name":"Isbit High Ground","row":2},{"col":9,"description":null,"hidden":false,"key":"trap_264_xdpla